{"ts":"2026-07-26T10:00:23.657Z","author":"harness:opencode","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"opencode","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-qapjw5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Changeset-to-item traceability gate: every merged changeset references a tracked pm item or an explicit waiver, enforced in CI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"AGENTS.md makes 'every code, docs, or test change must be linked to a pm item' a non-negotiable, but nothing machine-enforces it: compliance depends on agent discipline and is invisible when it degrades. Add a CI gate that extracts pm-id references from PR title/body and commit messages of a changeset, requires at least one resolvable active-or-terminal item id (or an explicit tracked waiver label), and fails otherwise. The reverse direction (which work produced a file) is pm-f86lth; this is the forward direction (no changeset lands untracked). Registers in the gate registry (pm-k6t4yb) with a negative-control fixture (a pm-id-free changeset must fail) and rides the same ratchet style as pm-kpftft. Completes the provenance half of the provable-history invariant: history proves what the tracker recorded; this proves the tracker recorded what the code did."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","context-management","governance","provenance","quality-gate","traceability"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-26T10:00:23.657Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T10:00:23.657Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:opencode"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"CI fails a changeset with no resolvable pm-id and no waiver; negative-control fixture proves the failure; waiver usage is itself a tracked, queryable event; gate registered in pm-k6t4yb with owner and failure taxonomy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make the code-to-tracker provenance loop closed and machine-enforced"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Every changeset is traversable to the work that authorized it; the graph gains evidence edges from real events instead of retrospective reconstruction"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"2026-07-26 ecosystem review found the forward direction of traceability unenforced while the reverse direction (pm-f86lth) and the gate infrastructure (pm-k6t4yb) are already tracked"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a7f68353c959740f0089eb25619b0ce24648c0d8db9bc0410b89eab0cd769011","message":"Filed by 2026-07-26 ecosystem review (pm-e9yevx); dedupe evidence: searches for changeset/commit/PR reference gates returned only reverse-direction pm-f86lth, registry pm-k6t4yb, and ratchet pm-kpftft"}
